Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: lamang pong ipaalala sa ating mga kababayan. This is a constitutional process. This is of paramount importance. And therefore, providing the reasons for the withdrawal of these witnesses need to be communicated as well. To the viewing public, Your Honor, Kailangan pong maintindihan ng ating mga kababayan ang naging hakbang ng prosekusyon kung bakit wini-withdraw ang mga pangalan ng ibang testigo para sa Articulo 4 and that is a threat. That is for the record only, Your Honor.

186
03:24:50,500 --> 03:24:55,150
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Noted. Court already made a ruling. Senator Judge Gaetano?

187
03:24:58,500 --> 03:27:00,810
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Mr. Senate President, Mr. Presiding Officer, I agree with you both and there's a solution to that. Let me start by I agree with the defense. Actually, I was going to stand up yesterday, but with all due respect to a good lawyer, Atty. Kapunan, and to the fact that my seatmate, Senator Migs, was very proud of her saying that she's his ninang, I did not stand up anymore. The problem with explaining why you're withdrawing is actually you are feeding to the Court something they did not testify to, and then something the defense cannot object to. So, and if it is a proffer or a tender, it is clear to everyone, and exclude yon, kaya ako nga lang nilalagay, but tama naman si Senate Press, si, um, presiding officer, it's akin, it's not the same, but, but dun kasi sa tender, So it's very clear to us it's unacceptable. So after the very eloquent manifestation of Atty. Kapunan yesterday, if I was a layman, I would think what you said, whether it was the agent John Mark, whether it was the second witness at NBI, was true. Kasi parang may summation. The same thing with you, the very able lead prosecutor and chairperson of the House Committee on Justice, diba? Having said that, I agree with you, this is an impeachment court. People have to know why. But I think we've been very lenient. No one except the spokesperson has spoken about the subjudice rule. So you can actually explain it in the presscon afterwards. If I may, no? Because nga, I was also observing yesterday, and

188
03:27:00,810 --> 03:27:19,650
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: I was saying, eh kuha ko yung defense, dadagdagan ko na yung witness ngayon, at every time iwi-withdraw, may chance akong i-explain bakit iwi-withdraw, then reinforce kung ano yung sinabi nung before. So I understand you completely, ma'am. People have to understand why it's not a sign of weakness. In fact, it's

189
03:27:19,650 --> 03:27:38,890
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: a sign that you've achieved your position. But we can do that in the press cons and other forums. But if you do it kasi here, walang chance yung prosecution to rebut that. Or if they do, it's one rebutting the other rather than the witness standing. So if I may offer that solution, Mr. Presiding Officer.

190
03:27:39,420 --> 03:27:49,080
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: As ruled by the Presiding Officer, henceforth, that will no longer be allowed. Senator Judge Pangilin, before Senator Judge Pia Cayetano.

191
03:27:49,300 --> 03:28:06,160
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: It's just a very quick manifestation. I was actually listening to the ruling of the Presiding Officer and initially I thought he would rule that the defense would likewise be given the opportunity to speak up.

192
03:28:07,160 --> 03:29:01,750
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: and, at some point, when they likewise have the opportunity to withdraw witnesses, I would like to think, Mr. Presiding Officer, that would have been the better approach because this is an Impeachment Court. We are not bound by technical rules, unlike court proceedings where lawyers are familiar and would really want, you know, to make it as orderly and as technical as possible. But again, I will yield to the ruling of the Chair. But just a reminder to everyone that technical rules of evidence do not apply strictly in impeachment court proceedings.

193
03:29:01,760 --> 03:29:35,460
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Precisely because nakikinig ang taong-bayan. Pagka-technical masyado, sa halip na lumalabas ang bawat punto. Hindi ko sinasabing hindi dapat magsalita ang defense. In fact, iyan ang original or initial suggestion at mungkahi ng ating Presiding Officer, na kung gustong magsalita ng defense din para tapatan iyong nabanggit ng prosecution, mas maganda sana. But I will yield. I just wanted that manifested, then I will yield to the ruling of the Chair.

194
03:29:35,460 --> 03:30:05,510
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We thank the good gentleman for his understanding and magnanimity. Given that counsel for respondent did not want the same benefit, it also saves on the Court's time. And as pointed out by Senator-Judge Alan, these words can be best expressed outside this Court so that we can manage the Court's time better, given that both parties have their respective spokespersons to discuss these matters. Counsel for respondent, you wanted to be recognized?

195
03:30:05,520 --> 03:30:07,030
Sheila C. Sison: Yes, Your Honor.

196
03:30:07,040 --> 03:30:30,630
Sheila C. Sison: May I just, very briefly, so that I won't take any more of the precious time of the Court and everyone who's here, with just a brief response to the lead prosecutor's counter-manifestation that this is because this is a constitutional procedure. We understand that when we—

197
03:30:30,640 --> 03:30:55,530
Sheila C. Sison: came here, mulat ang aming mga mata na pumunta rito at alam namin na ito ay isang constitutional mechanism. Kaya nga, iyong sinasabi ko kanina at ang aking kahilingan lamang ay nakasandig doon sa prinsipyong iyon: na dahil ito ay isang constitutional mechanism, kailangan siguraduhin natin na balanse at patas iyong lahat ng

198
03:30:55,530 --> 03:31:47,450
Sheila C. Sison: magaganap. At hindi ko—I find it difficult to understand how manifestations containing assertions that are laden with conclusions and personal advocacy, and obviously one-sided advocacy of either party, would help the Court arrive at the proper determination of whether the respondent is guilty or not guilty of the charges contained in the Articles of Impeachment. Hindi rin po ito in response po to our good Senator Pangilinan. Hindi po technical rules ang ini-invoke ko rito, kundi iyong—actually, it's substantive dahil ito ay nakasandig sa ating Saligang Batas. Salamat po.

199
03:31:47,460 --> 03:31:51,160
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Noted. Senator-Judge Pia Cayetano is recognized. What is your pleasure, ma'am?

200
03:31:57,650 --> 03:32:07,090
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: I would just like to support the ruling of the presiding officer, cautioning both prosecution and defense.

201
03:32:09,200 --> 03:32:28,370
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: I too noticed the esteemed Atty. Lorna Kapunan's lengthy explanation on the withdrawal of the witnesses. But because she is Lorna Kapunan, nakikinig ako in the same way na even if I don't know some of your names, makikinig ako sa inyo. Rest assured,

202
03:32:28,670 --> 03:33:09,330
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: I think it's her first time to also stand up so I was being very patient in listening to her but I did take note of some statements that sabi ko parang conclusions na to or excessive explanation of of her observations, which I didn't think were proper. So, okay naman, okay na yun, tapos na yun, pero moving forward nga, Mr. Presiding Officer, I agree with you. And I just need to put this on record, kasi nga, sinasabing huwag tayo masyadong technical, pero, to a certain extent, kailangan naman ho natin tingnan naman yung rules natin, kasi,

203
03:33:13,010 --> 03:33:23,450
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So, I want to read into the record. This might be a paraphrase na nung sinabi niya ha, kasi sinasummarize namin ng team ko yung statements.

204
03:33:25,060 --> 03:33:59,920
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Anyway, hindi ko na mahanap sa phone ko dahil kahapon pa iyon. But I recall—and feel free to correct me, but this is a minor thing naman—parang dinescribe niya kung bakit: why won't Atty. Lopez go to court? Because the defense already showed the video where he was crying and complaining. So that's an observation from Atty. Kapunan. She's not the witness. She shouldn't be the one telling the judges that he was crying and complaining.

205
03:33:59,930 --> 03:34:18,700
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Trabaho po iyon ng abogado na i-elicit iyon doon sa witness na mape-presenta. So iyon po iyong reason kung bakit hindi puwede iyon. We're not being technical, but—

206
03:34:18,710 --> 03:35:20,760
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: neither of the lawyers here are allowed to stand up and be the one to explain what you are experiencing. That is the job for the witness to do. Your job is to ask the witness questions. Iyon iyon. So to be clear, it's not being technical, but it's making sure that magawa ninyo iyong trabaho ninyo nang maayos at magtanong tayo nang maayos sa witnesses. Kung hindi na pala siya papupuntahin, no need na to say kung ano iyong na-observe, kasi nga hindi na sa inyo iyon as lawyers. Iyon lang naman po. Again, my utmost respect for Atty. Kapunan and to all of you. You're all doing a great job. Like I said, once in a while, we will be called out—even I. I tell the Presiding Officer, call me out pag sumobra ako, pag medyo nag-exceed tayo ng authority natin, because we're all just trying to do our jobs here. So thank you again, everyone, for your time and patience. Thank you, Presiding Officer.

207
03:35:21,760 --> 03:35:47,190
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Chair, in humility, accepts the presiding officer's lapses in this regard, as twice pointed out by Senator-Judge Pia Cayetano already. The chair will be more mindful in the future, but I also ask the parties to also be equally. In case the Chair forgets or is unable to point it out on the part of either party, should this happen again. Any other points?

208
03:35:47,230 --> 03:35:47,710
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: One

209
03:35:47,710 --> 03:36:01,530
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: last manifestation from the Honorable Luistro without prejudice to another manifestation from Council for Responding.

210
03:36:04,330 --> 03:37:26,860
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: The Honorable Impeachment Court has been very much fair in as far as this issue is concerned. As a matter of fact, the presiding officer even asked the lead defense counsel if she would like to avail of the same opportunity to explain the reason for the withdrawal in the event the defense would be withdrawing likewise their witnesses. Also, Your Honor, may I just add, and with all due respect to honorable Senator Pia Cayetano, the intention of the prosecution is never to abuse the time of the impeachment court. It is never to influence the senator judges, neither is it to influence the viewing public. The explanation was a statement of the position of the prosecution and of course it is anticipated that the same is adverse to the other party because it is apparent. That we are in the prosecution side while the opposing counsel is on the defense side but nonetheless let me reiterate and put on record your honor the purpose is not to influence the senator judges neither is it to influence the viewing public it is only a statement of position of the prosecution for withdrawing the names of the prosecution's witnesses your honor

211
03:37:26,860 --> 03:37:29,520
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: noted and the ruling of the court stands on the matter

212
03:37:30,290 --> 03:38:02,470
Sheila C. Sison: Council correspondent. Brief counter-manifestation, Your Honor. I thank the lead prosecutor for mentioning that the same courtesy was earlier offered to the defense with respect to providing lengthy discourses or manifestations before this court. But I think the point essentially that I'm trying to make is that we're not Asking the court for any advantage. What we're merely asking is fairness. That's all, Your Honor. Thank you.

213
03:38:03,420 --> 03:38:08,920
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Same answer noted and the court stands by its ruling. Any other matters to be taken up from the senator judges?

214
03:38:11,250 --> 03:38:20,070
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: There being none, no other business to be taken up, the trial is hereby adjourned until 2 p.m. of Monday, July 20, 2026.

215
03:38:20,810 --> 03:38:21,490
Sheila C. Sison: Thank you.
